_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- sai-task-v1:R10-T041 -->\n\n## Student: Krrish\n\n**Task:** R10-T041 · 1 of 10\n**Repository:** https://github.com/S-AI-Projects/free-programming-books\n**Assigned working branch:** `student/e26b07f1180`\n\n## Goal\n\nExtract display name, URL, category and available metadata while preserving the original line number. Selected entries: AI School: https://lillytechsystems.com/ai-school/; AIMarket Courses: https://alexar76.github.io/aimarket-courses/; CheatGrid: https://www.cheatgrid.com/roadmaps\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read the contribution rules and the exact learning-resource list section in courses/free-courses-en.md. Work on these entries: AI School: https://lillytechsystems.com/ai-school/; AIMarket Courses: https://alexar76.github.io/aimarket-courses/; CheatGrid: https://www.cheatgrid.com/roadmaps.\n2. Implement tools/course_checks/r10-t041.py for the assigned check. Scope its input to this file/section; retain source line numbers in the result.\n3. Create offline fixtures for the stated success and failure cases. Live requests, where relevant, must use a timeout, low concurrency and a small fixed entry list.\n4. Make a catalogue correction only when the evidence proves it is needed; the parser/checker and its tested report are the required contribution even when the source entries are already correct.\n5. Create the checks specified below and run `python3 tools/course_checks/r10-t041.py --self-test`. Save inputs, expected versus actual results and tool versions in work/R10-T041/; a check must exit non-zero when an assertion fails.\n6. Commit the repository change on branch R10-T041; prepare a PR to the organisation fork explaining the result and linking the checks. Keep each task independently reviewable. Remove work/R10-T041/ from a later upstream branch.\n\n## Done when\n\n☐ A fenced-code fake link is ignored, a URL containing a fragment is preserved, and each selected real entry maps back to its source line.\n☐ The checker has a --self-test mode whose failing assertions produce a nonzero exit.\n☐ No link is removed solely because a single automated request failed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Additional task guidance</summary>\n\n\nAdditional curated task guidance\n\nItem:\ncourses/free-courses-en.md\n\nTask type:\nStructured parser\n\nCode change (goes into the PR):\ntools/course_checks/r10-t041.py and its focused fixtures (new organisation-fork tooling); courses/free-courses-en.md: only evidence-backed entry corrections. Include a README for the checker with the actual selected entries.\n\nAutomated check:\npython3 tools/course_checks/r10-t041.py --self-test\n\nPrerequisites:\nPython 3 with its standard library; internet/browser access only for the small manual verification step. No API key is required for offline checks.\n\nUpstream PR rules:\nFollow the language list, ordering and free-access rules. Confirm redirects in a browser before removing a resource; a rate limit is not a dead link. Submit coursework to the organisation fork first; keep work/ evidence out of any later upstream PR. Upstream acceptance is not a grading requirement. Policy: https://github.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/blob/b4c4cc4040b614d2aca81ad5f2bcd92ed3d422ec/docs/CONTRIBUTING.md\n\nSource (pinned):\nhttps://github.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/blob/b4c4cc4040b614d2aca81ad5f2bcd92ed3d422ec/courses/free-courses-en.md#L1\n\nChange:\nReplaces the shared task template with an item-specific contribution brief.\n\nPR destination:\nOrganisation-fork tooling; evidence-backed catalogue edits may be proposed upstream\n\n\n</details>\n\n## Submission checklist\n\n- [ ] Complete this task and its checks.\n- [ ] Add the required evidence and link your pull request here.\n- [ ] Select this **S-AI-Projects fork** as the PR base repository.\n- [ ] Request instructor review.\n\nKeep this PR focused on this task. Do not submit assignment PRs to the upstream repository.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/S-AI-Projects/free-programming-books/issues/5/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/S-AI-Projects/free-programming-books/issues/5/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}